<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A matrix with a given area scale factor</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Give a matrix \(M\) with no zero entries such that the image of every shape under \(M\) has \({@s@}\) times the area of the shape and [[if test="is(o=1)"]]the same orientation[[else]]the reverse orientation[[/if]].</p><div>\(M = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The area scale factor is \(|\det M|\), and a negative determinant reverses the orientation. So you need \(\det M = {@tg@}\).</p><p>Choose three entries that are not 0 and solve for the fourth. For example, \({@m1@}\) has determinant \({@determinant(m1)@}\), and so does \({@m2@}\). Many other matrices work.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
/* Design: construct-an-instance pattern (graded by property). Source: original. 5 same and 5 reversed orientation. Model answers m1, m2 have det = tg and no zero entry; zm has a zero; wm has det -tg; |det gm| # s. */
slist: [[2,1],[3,-1],[4,1],[5,-1],[6,1],[8,-1],[3,1],[10,-1],[12,1],[2,-1]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
s: slist[ix][1]; o: slist[ix][2]; tg: s*o;
m1: if o=1 then matrix([s+1,1],[1,1]) else matrix([1,s+1],[1,1]);
m2: matrix([1,1],[1,1+tg]);
zm: matrix([tg,0],[0,1]);
wm: matrix([m1[1,1],m1[1,2]],[-m1[2,1],-m1[2,2]]);
gm: if o=1 then matrix([s+2,1],[1,1]) else matrix([1,s+2],[1,1]);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, s={@s@}, orientation {@o@}</text>
  </questionnote>
